                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Unblemished splurging. [/h1] \n\nHearing UsHiRoMiYaAaAaaaa BATORAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA in my head 24-7 (again) playing this masterpiece fighting game based on peak fiction. An overwhelmingly faithful Umineko fighter is the wildest shit to think of existing but holy hell is it like ketamine to an autistic VN whore. It's all there: the banger music, the iconic voices, the detailed recreations of the settings in all their glory, not to mention the gorgeous spritework and animations to boot.\n\nI don't particularly enjoy tag-team fighters. I usually feel like the actual system of switching characters doesn't work when there's no real incentive to engage with it. It always comes down to a lack of design direction to me. Why deliberate over good combos of characters in a fight when you can smash the shit out of your opponent just fine with one?\n\nBut with Golden Fantasia, the way the special meters are built up on the character that you AREN'T currently using on the field makes it make sense. It actually encourages you to switch strategically back-and-forth between the character combo you pick which results in genuinely fun and dynamic gameplay, and its super effective. I feel like Umineko especially lends itself to that approach directly because of the themes of its story, how its only possible to create a universe with more than one person. In short, without love, it cannot be seen. All that jazz. It's a great way of mechanically mirroring that sentiment in the purest sense possible, and more than that, it's just plain fucking FUNNN.\n\nThe only issue I kinda have is the controls are a little weird to get used to. You'll definitely need to spend time in the training mode to get the hang of it, but once you do it'll shortly click, and its really not that big of a deal. Don't be afraid either to look for help online with setting up your controller in a way that feels good for you. I got my PS4 controller to work well after only a few minutes of dedication. This is my layout:\nA = Butt3\nB = Butt1\nC = Butt2\nD = Butt4\nTaunt = Butt7\nStart = Butt8\n\nNow I'm off to beg to the weeb gods in my heart for an equally awesome Higurashi fighter someday ughhhhh. Have a nice day, see you again~",
